  "notes": "Waiver statement (Exhibit A), cash basis, period 10/1/21-9/30/22. General, Street and Emergency Medical funds governmental; Sewer Fund business-type, rolled forward in business_type: 16,572.37 + 7,549.23 - 7,178.48 = 16,943.12. Governmental roll-forward: 132,660.40 + 37,496.84 - 29,460.55 = 140,696.69. Governmental cash balances are the line 3 / line 28 subtotals (net cash + investments); investments are CDs and savings (p3 schedule, total 104,070.92 all funds). Sewer 'Local Receipts: Other' cell is faint (reads 7,540.23 or 7,549.23); 7,549.23 taken because both the Sewer Total Receipts 7,549.23 and the line 18 Total 15,541.13 require it. 'Local Receipts: Other' split by column (governmental 7,991.90 / Sewer 7,549.23); the Sewer piece stays other (no page evidence it is sewer charges; user ruling 2026-11-12). Sewer 'Debt Service' 3,569.00 is printed on the Governmental Debt Service row but in the Sewer Fund column (sewer loan, 50,150.11 outstanding, p3), so it is business-type, as in FY2023. No transfers (p3 schedule blank). County Treasurer balances (383.55 at 10/1/21, 389.17 at 9/30/22) are memo items, not in cash. No detail schedules beyond Exhibit A; detail is per fund column. Read pages 1-3 of 3"
